@@@ note
The worst case: a '---' line is a setext underline, which reaches *backwards* and turns the
line above it into a heading — so the corruption lands on text that was already emitted and
looked safe. It is also a thematic break. See #6.

@@@ input
alpha bravo charlie --- delta echo foxtrot.

@@@ wrap 80
alpha bravo charlie --- delta echo foxtrot.

@@@ wrap 6
alpha
bravo
charlie
\---
delta
echo
foxtrot.

@@@ unwrap
alpha bravo charlie --- delta echo foxtrot.
